    rdfs:comment "Nouhad Wadie Haddad (born 20 November 1934 or 21 November 1935), known professionally as Fairuz, is a Lebanese singer. She is widely considered an iconic vocalist and one of the most celebrated singers in the Arab world, as well as a symbol of modern Lebanon. She is popularly known as \"The Bird of the East\", \"The Cedar of Lebanon\", \"The Moon's Neighbor\", \"The Voice of Lebanon\", and \"Our Ambassador to the Stars\", among others." .

